     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi this might be a bit off topic, but is anyone aware of efforts to &quot;combine&quot; the results of presence only models and occupancy models in an &quot;ensemble&quot; modeling framework?  What does combine mean?  Whatever you think it means..<div><br></div><div>I found two papers in the literature, but neither are particularly statistical........</div><div><br></div><div><div>Albanese et al. 2013.  Using occupancy and species distribution models to assess the conservation status and habitat use of the goldline darter (Percina aurolineata) in Georgia, USA Ecology of Freshwater Fish 2014: 23: 347–359</div></div><div><br></div><div>Peterman et al. 2013 Using species distribution and occupancy modeling to guide survey efforts and assess species status. Journal for Nature Conservation. <br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m not saying it&#39;s a good idea to combine the two types of models just want to know if anyone;s done it well. Who and why are we doing this?  long story has to do with bats.   </div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Robin</div><div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">Using</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">species</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">distribution</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">and</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">occupancy</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">modeling</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">to</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">guide</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">survey</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">efforts</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">and</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">assess</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">species</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px;margin:0px;color:transparent;white-space:pre;opacity:0.5;text-align:center;font-size:17.9328px;font-family:serif\">status</div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
